      {
        "id": 49148,
        "name": "Rabit",
        "username": "Rabit",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/rabit/{size}/7330_2.png",
        "created_at": "2012-12-14T12:36:41.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"Odin_Knight\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/odin_knight/48/2548_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Odin_Knight:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Why don't you just flip the rulebook and make sure to follow the turn actions posted there?I always leave the rulebook visible to all players, so we have no problems in the turn scheme…</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Yeah, that's something we do with the demos, and it usually helps a lot. Magic players sometimes have the reflex to go to the deck. I know I did for a while, but I've definitely gotten over that.  <img src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/images/emoji/apple/sunglasses.png?v=12\" title=\":sunglasses:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":sunglasses:\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\"></p>",
